# One room password, one broker user.
#
# The password gates the broker; it does not separate members. Every session uses
# the `cluster` user, so any member can read every task and result, dispatch tasks,
# and use any worker id. What remains is enforced in the payload by the extension:
# a worker ignores tasks not addressed to it, and the orchestrator ignores results
# whose workerId differs from the pinned worker.
#
# Isolation between members would require one credential per device (mTLS with
# use_identity_as_username, or per-machine passwords), which is the design this
# replaced.

user cluster
topic readwrite pi/v1/#
